1. dotnet/wpf — WpfGfx (MIL: Media Integration Layer)
   https://github.com/dotnet/wpf
   Licence: MIT
   Copyright (c) .NET Foundation and Contributors

   Ported/adapted algorithms (reverse-engineered against d2d1.dll, which shares
   the MIL geometry code, and cross-checked against the open WpfGfx source):
     * crates/d2d/src/geometry/fill_tess.rs   — CScanner sweep + CTessellator band
       triangulation (WpfGfx/core/geometry/scanner.cpp, tessellate.cpp)
     * crates/d2d/src/geometry/aatess.rs      — CAATessellator single-sweep AA
       tessellation (same scanner.cpp / tessellate.cpp, no-intersection path)
     * crates/d2d/src/geometry/stroke.rs      — CWidener / CSimplePen stroke widener
       (WpfGfx/core/geometry/strokefigure.{cpp,h}, cpen.cpp)
     * crates/d2d/src/geometry/dash.rs        — CDasher (strokefigure.{cpp,h})
     * crates/d2d/src/geometry/milbezier.rs   — HFD Bézier "cracker" (bezier.{h,cpp})
     * crates/d2d/src/pixels/copy_tess.rs     — CHwRasterizer trapezoid-fringe AA
       (the opaque COPY-blend fill path)
     * crates/d2d/src/geometry/combine/{scanner,sweep,intersect,exact}.rs —
       CScanner region scan (chain building, sweep, junctions, robust segment
       intersection) and its reconstructor, ported for Outline/Combine/Compare
       figure structure (WpfGfx/core/geometry/scanner.{cpp,h},
       LineSegmentIntersection.{cpp,h}, ExactArithmetic.{cpp,h},
       IntervalArithmetic.h, Boolean.{cpp,h}; WpfGfx/common/shared/heap.h),
       checked against d2d1.dll
   (The rest of crates/d2d/src/geometry/combine/ implements the same MIL
   combine/scanline algorithm but was reconstructed from the d2d1.dll binary, not
   copied from WpfGfx source; it is noted here for completeness.)

